The hands are compute, model, and user.
A calling has four parts. No calling, no run.
Compute works from the rules and the books. It does not guess. A miss goes to the model with a top list, then to the user.
Derived faces are compute's, with an author. A miss goes up.
Sign is a compute and model check. Approve, lock, and promote stay with the user.
The clerk hands a cold boot for the book. Pages 0001 through 0009 port a rule and take a local change.
The calling is read from the command list. Where the rule is seated is still open.
Local mode: the user engages it and compute activates it. The shape is still open.
Still open: an author on each section, the two user modes, the sign line in AGENTS, and what >keep means.
05.01 on this page said one ask names one caller. This batch takes four parts on one act.
